      "start_seconds": 1.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "hmm, you know, doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.55,
      "end_seconds": 15.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "that's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.24,
      "end_seconds": 35.04,
      "duration_seconds": 17.8,
      "text": "Um, so... the room spinning. That's why I came. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.02,
      "end_seconds": 38.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.82,
      "end_seconds": 43.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Oh, for one week, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.9,
      "end_seconds": 49.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.89,
      "end_seconds": 58.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "it's all the time there's a recent cold as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.12,
      "end_seconds": 75.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "And what about weakness, hearing loss, double vision or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.44,
      "end_seconds": 80.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I mean, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.91,
      "end_seconds": 84.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.17,
      "end_seconds": 89.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.89,
      "end_seconds": 94.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.94,
      "end_seconds": 100.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.02,
      "end_seconds": 103.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.02,
      "end_seconds": 109.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.14,
      "end_seconds": 113.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "And And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.79,
      "end_seconds": 117.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.64,
      "end_seconds": 121.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.87,
      "end_seconds": 130.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.82,
      "end_seconds": 133.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "alright, are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.56,
      "end_seconds": 138.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.94,
      "end_seconds": 141.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "right, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.74,
      "end_seconds": 155.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about ten years i've had low haemoglobin for two years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.83,
      "end_seconds": 164.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "yes, low haemoglobin is known to us, good to have that clear have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.37,
      "end_seconds": 169.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.85,
      "end_seconds": 173.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.84,
      "end_seconds": 187.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.6,
      "text": "So, I take amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day. Iron tablets. I take it once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.77,
      "end_seconds": 204.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.36,
      "end_seconds": 218.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.38,
      "end_seconds": 253.68,
      "duration_seconds": 14.3,
      "text": "okay: heart rate 83, BMI works out to 26.4, weight 78 kilos and temperature 37.0, respiratory rate 15, height 172 centimetres, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, blood pressure 121 over 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.71,
      "end_seconds": 256.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.66,
      "end_seconds": 260.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.14,
      "end_seconds": 265.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.73,
      "end_seconds": 269.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.52,
      "end_seconds": 287.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "I can see a fine jerking of the eyes to the left and your walking is a little unsteady"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.51,
      "end_seconds": 293.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.17,
      "end_seconds": 328.74,
      "duration_seconds": 26.57,
      "text": "so where does that leave us? I can't pin this down yet we're looking at an inner-ear balance problem such as vestibular neuritis or benign positional vertigo we should do a positional test for vertigo. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for dizziness i'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.71,
      "end_seconds": 357.8,
      "duration_seconds": 27.09,
      "text": "Let's use prochlorperazine, 5 milligrams, three times a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. It's for nausea and vertigo. Start moving around gently as soon as you can, since resting too long slows recovery. We'll refer you to to the balance clinic. Do get help quickly if you get double vision, weakness or trouble speaking. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.38,
      "end_seconds": 362.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.29,
      "end_seconds": 364.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
